import duckdb
con = duckdb.connect(database="splink_temp_workspace.duckdb")
con.execute("SET memory_limit = '24GB';")
con.execute("SET temp_directory = './duckdb_spill_dir.tmp';")
db_api = DuckDBAPI(connection=con)
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{Global Aggregation Engine}
\label{sec:agg_engine_impl}

The \texttt{aggregation} package (\texttt{em/aggregation/}) implements the vector-space aggregation approach:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{ProcessorRegistry}: Maps type strings (\texttt{"numerical"}, \texttt{"categorical"}, \texttt{"set\_union"}) to \texttt{ColumnProcessor} subclasses.
    \item \textbf{ColumnProcessor} (abstract base): \texttt{get\_agg\_func()}, \texttt{fit\_vocab(df1, df2)}, \texttt{post\_process(df\_agg)}.
    \item \textbf{Aggregator}: Coordinates multiple processors; \texttt{fit(df1, df2)} builds vocabularies; \texttt{transform(df, label)} groups by \texttt{unique\_id\_col}, applies agg funcs, runs post-processors.
    \item \textbf{Outputs per type}:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item \texttt{numerical}: mean, min, max (for range overlap comparison)
        \item \texttt{categorical}: token list + frequency vector (for cosine/Jaccard)
        \item \texttt{set\_union}: union of set elements across records
    \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

Usage in \texttt{agg\_music.ipynb} (\Cref{sec:behavioural_agg}):
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python, caption={Aggregator Instantiation for Music Data}, label=lst:agg_music]
type_groups = ["numerical", "categorical", "set_union"]
col_groups = [
    ["numerical_noisy"],
    ["categorical_title", "categorical_album", "language", "categorical_number"],
    ["year_options"]
]
agg = Aggregator(type_groups=type_groups, col_groups=col_groups, unique_id_col="artist")
agg.fit(df1_processed, df2_processed)
aggregated_df1 = agg.transform(df1_processed, "music_catalog_df1")
aggregated_df2 = agg.transform(df2_processed, "music_catalog_df2")
\end{lstlisting}